language sdl-mvp1-exercise version 0.1.

scenario GlobalStopFlow.
condition GlobalStopFlowReady.
condition GlobalStopFlowContinue.
condition GlobalStopFlowReject.
outcome GlobalStopFlowCompleted.
outcome GlobalStopFlowRejected.
step GlobalStopFlowBucking.
step GlobalStopFlowMachine.
step GlobalStopFlowLab.
step GlobalStopFlowResult.
step GlobalStopFlowFailure.
step GlobalStopFlowSuccess.
step GlobalStopFlowRoute.
step GlobalStopSendMachine.
step GlobalStopSendBucking.
step GlobalStopFlowPartial.
condition StopRouteDirect.
condition StopRouteViaBucking.
condition StopLabPresent.
condition StopLabAbsent.
condition StopCoordinationPartial.
outcome StopPartiallyObserved.

GlobalStopFlow illustrates RequestSoftwareStop.
GlobalStopFlow exercises AuthoritativeMachineState.
GlobalStopFlow starts-when GlobalStopFlowReady.
GlobalStopFlow starts-at GlobalStopFlowRoute.
GlobalStopFlowReady describes "A valid connected client requests an identified software stop occurrence.".
GlobalStopFlowContinue describes "The previous operation succeeded and the next step's declared contract preconditions remain true; exact predicates are an executable-language gap.".
GlobalStopFlowReject describes "Validation, authority, applicability or operation failure prevents continuation; preserve prior valid state and report the specific reason.".
GlobalStopFlowCompleted describes "The stated design path completed under its explicit obligations; this is not an observed test result.".
GlobalStopFlowRejected describes "The path terminated without claiming the requested change succeeded; failures remain observable.".
GlobalStopFlow preserves DiagnosticsSurviveStop.
GlobalStopFlow preserves ServerBoundAuthority.
GlobalStopFlow preserves DurableFactsRetained.
GlobalStopFlowRoute describes "A routed operator stop may target Machine directly or Bucking for local handling and forwarding; Bucking absence never blocks the direct path.".
GlobalStopFlowRoute proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowFailure when GlobalStopFlowReject.
GlobalStopFlowRoute proceeds-to GlobalStopSendMachine when StopRouteDirect.
GlobalStopFlowRoute proceeds-to GlobalStopSendBucking when StopRouteViaBucking.
GlobalStopSendMachine calls RouteBrowserCommand within BuckingWeb.
GlobalStopSendMachine proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowMachine when GlobalStopFlowContinue.
GlobalStopSendMachine proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowPartial when StopCoordinationPartial.
GlobalStopSendBucking calls RouteBrowserCommand within BuckingWeb.
GlobalStopSendBucking proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowBucking when GlobalStopFlowContinue.
GlobalStopSendBucking proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowPartial when StopCoordinationPartial.
GlobalStopFlowBucking calls HandleBuckingStop within BuckingService.
GlobalStopFlowBucking describes "Optional forwarding retains stop_id and invalidates local normal work.".
GlobalStopFlowBucking proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowPartial when StopCoordinationPartial.
GlobalStopFlowBucking proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowMachine when GlobalStopFlowContinue.
GlobalStopFlowMachine calls HandleMachineStop within MachineService.
GlobalStopFlowMachine describes "Deduplicate by service session/retention; reject conflicting retained payload; invalidate old generations.".
GlobalStopFlowMachine proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowPartial when StopCoordinationPartial.
GlobalStopFlowMachine proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowLab when StopLabPresent.
GlobalStopFlowMachine proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowResult when StopLabAbsent.
GlobalStopFlowLab calls StopLabAutomation within MachineLab.
GlobalStopFlowLab describes "Cancel configured automation, preserve observers/ledger.".
GlobalStopFlowLab proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowPartial when StopCoordinationPartial.
GlobalStopFlowLab proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowResult when GlobalStopFlowContinue.
GlobalStopFlowResult calls DeliverDurableOutcome within BuckingUI.
GlobalStopFlowResult describes "Report software stop without claiming certified physical E-stop.".
GlobalStopFlowResult proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowPartial when StopCoordinationPartial.
GlobalStopFlowResult proceeds-to GlobalStopFlowSuccess when GlobalStopFlowContinue.
GlobalStopFlowFailure finishes GlobalStopFlow with GlobalStopFlowRejected.
GlobalStopFlowSuccess finishes GlobalStopFlow with GlobalStopFlowCompleted.
GlobalStopFlowBucking emits MachineRequests through MachineServiceUpstream.
GlobalStopFlowMachine receives MachineRequests through MachineServiceUpstream.
GlobalStopSendMachine emits MachineRequests through MachineServiceUpstream.
GlobalStopSendBucking emits BuckingRequests through BuckingServiceUpstream.
StopRouteDirect describes "Validated routing selects MachineService directly; Bucking availability is irrelevant.".
StopRouteViaBucking describes "Validated routing selects BuckingService local handling and forwarding with the same stop_id.".
StopLabPresent describes "Machine local handling succeeded and configured Lab automation participates.".
StopLabAbsent describes "Machine local handling succeeded and no Lab automation participates.".
StopCoordinationPartial describes "A downstream handler or delivery failed or remains unknown after dispatch; retain all already handled stop effects and report per-owner outcome.".
GlobalStopFlowPartial finishes GlobalStopFlow with StopPartiallyObserved.
StopPartiallyObserved describes "Do not claim every participant stopped or undo an accepted stop. Further per-owner recovery is required; no physical safety conclusion follows.".
